.\" Source: src/wd-record.c
.TH "WD-RECORD" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
wd-record \- record receiver streams with WSPRdaemon timing support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wd-record
.RI "[options] data-destination"
.SH STATUS
.B Maintained by N5TNL
.SH DESCRIPTION
wd-record is a recorder derived from pcmrecord with WSPRdaemon timing,
sample-count, and optional BPSK synchronization features. It records RTP PCM
into WAVE files and Opus into Ogg, or supplies streams to stdout or commands.
Its option semantics differ from the current pcmrecord; in particular, -L and
-x remain separate here.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-c, \-\-stdout, \-\-catmode"
Write one selected stream to standard output.
.TP
.B "\-e command, \-\-exec command"
Start a shell command per session and pipe the stream to it. Supports the $
substitutions described in pcmrecord(1); single-quote the argument.
.TP
.B "\-d directory, \-\-directory directory"
Set existing recording directory. Default current directory.
.TP
.B "\-S ssrc, \-\-ssrc ssrc"
Select one SSRC.
.TP
.B "\-o source, \-\-source source"
Restrict reception to a network source.
.TP
.B "\-r, \-\-raw"
Omit PCM WAVE headers; Opus retains Ogg framing.
.TP
.B "\-f, \-\-flush"
Flush stream/Ogg output promptly.
.TP
.B "\-s, \-\-subdirs, \-\-subdirectories"
Create per-SSRC/date subdirectories.
.TP
.B "\-j, \-\-jt"
Use K1JT-style filenames.
.TP
.B "\-L seconds, \-\-lengthlimit seconds, \-\-limit seconds"
Set recurring recording segment duration. Default zero disables this limit.
.TP
.B "\-x seconds, \-\-max_length seconds"
Set a separate finite sample-count recording limit. Mark sessions complete
when their files close, and exit when all known sessions are complete. Unlike
pcmrecord in this revision, this is not an alias for -L.
.TP
.B "\-m seconds, \-\-mintime seconds, \-\-minfiletime seconds"
Minimum qualifying segment duration; default 0.2 seconds.
.TP
.B "\-t seconds, \-\-timeout seconds"
Idle timeout before session closure; default 20 seconds, integer argument.
.TP
.B "\-W, \-\-wd_mode"
Enable WSPRdaemon mode, align recordings, and use JT filenames. If no -L limit
has yet been selected, sets it to 60 seconds.
.TP
.B "\-E samples, \-\-error samples"
Force a signed sample-count error for diagnostics.
.TP
.B "\-q pathname, \-\-wd_errors pathname"
Select the WSPRdaemon error-log file.
.TP
.B "\-Y seconds, \-\-wd_tolerance seconds"
Set WSPRdaemon synchronization tolerance; default two seconds.
.TP
.B "\-\-sync\-ssrc ssrc"
Select the BPSK synchronization-channel SSRC.
.TP
.B "\-\-sync\-frequency Hz"
Set BPSK synchronization frequency in Hz.
.TP
.B "\-\-sync\-record"
Also record the synchronization channel.
.TP
.B "\-\-sync\-pretrigger samples"
Set BPSK pretrigger offset in samples.
.TP
.B "\-\-no\-output"
Enable diagnostic operation without normal recording output.
.TP
.B "\-\-filter\-500"
Enable the experimental 500 Hz notch filter.
.TP
.B "\-\-leaky\-folding"
Enable experimental leaky folding in the synchronization processing.
.TP
.B "\-\-leaky\-folding\-filter coefficient"
Set the leaky-folding coefficient between zero and one. Default 0.99; invalid
values revert to 0.99.
.TP
.B "\-l locale, \-\-locale locale"
Select locale, initially LANG.
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-verbose"
Increase diagnostics.
.TP
.B "\-V, \-\-version"
Print program and WSPRdaemon-mode version information, then exit.
.SH NOTES
Use synchronization and forced-error options only with a matching timing
setup. stdout/exec override ordinary file naming modes. This program has no
--reacquire option. Confirm finite-limit, restart, and synchronization
behavior for the intended WSPRdaemon deployment before unattended use.
.SH EXAMPLES
Record aligned 60-second WSPRdaemon segments:
.PP
.nf
wd\-record \-W \-L 60 \-d /var/tmp/wd\-record wspr\-pcm.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
pcmrecord(1), jt-decoded(1), radiod(8)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
